Write Python source only no semicolons. Script takes directory argv1. Iterate pathlib.Path(directory).rglob('*.dna'), parse Bio.SeqIO.read(path,'snapgene'), count each first label qualifier using collections.Counter. Catch parse errors and record filename and error separately. Print JSON {'labels':counter.most_common(),'errors':errors,'files':count}. No sequence output, no writes, no subprocess. Under30lines.
RESPONSE
import sys, json, pathlib, Bio.SeqIO, collections
d = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])
c = collections.Counter()
e = []
for p in d.rglob('*.dna'):
    try:
        r = Bio.SeqIO.read(p, 'snapgene')
        c[r.metadata.get('label', '')] += 1
    except Exception as x:
        e.append({'file': str(p), 'error': str(x)})
print(json.dumps({'labels': c.most_common(), 'errors': e, 'files': len(list(d.rglob('*.dna')))})